  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Decision\\n\\n**The observation cursor in this integration is a single, global, filter-independent durable position** — per Ordarium's published contract for the pinned version (`@ordarium/core@1.3.1` / `@ordarium/ledger-sqlite@1.3.1`), the \\\"state change feed\\\" cursor introduced as `ORD-BOOT-0`/`ORD-BOOT-0.1`.\\n\\n**The per-subscription reading in `docs/engineering/notes/cursor-note.md` does not apply.**\\n\\n## What the \\\"observation cursor\\\" is here\\n\\n\\\"Observation\\\" is Ordarium's term for incremental reading of committed state revisions after a durable position:\\n\\n- `@ordarium/core/dist/src/state.d.ts` — `StateStore.changes(...)`: *\\\"Incremental observation of committed state revisions after a durable position (ORD-BOOT-0).\\\"*\\n- `@ordarium/core/dist/src/types.d.ts` — `StateChangePage.cursor` is *always present* and is *\\\"Opaque, **filter-independent** durable position of the last delivered change.\\\"* `StateChangeFilter.namespace` only *\\\"Restrict[s] observation to one namespace; absent observes every namespace.\\\"*\\n- `@ordarium/ledger-sqlite/dist/src/index.js` `changes()` — the cursor is validated against the **global** high-water mark, not the namespace's: *\\\"the cursor is a ",
